# macOS listener handoff recovery

## Observed failure

An operator authenticated to PLANK at the sign-in screen, then selected a
different macOS desktop account. The old sign-in worker exited. The new,
admitted desktop worker received POSIX EADDRINUSE while binding the TLS control
port and exited cleanly. No listener remained afterward. launchd deferred its
KeepAlive restart because the Aqua domain was on-demand-only. The existing
coordinator had already marked its successful kickstart request finished.

An explicitly authorized kickstart of only the current desktop job restored
discovery without a reboot, installation or permission change. The exact old
socket state at bind failure was not captured; TCP TIME_WAIT is a hypothesis,
not established evidence. Product logs lacked the numeric listener failure;
the OS unified log contained it.

## Scope and implementation

Developed on `macos-listener-recovery`, based on the released mainline. Keep the
existing root coordinator and launchd jobs; add no service or persistent watcher.

- After the exact admitted desktop process exits and its lease is released,
  re-arm the existing startup budget for the same current UID/audit session.
- Share ten explicit starts across launch races and worker failures. Retry
  delays are 1, 2, 4, 8 and at most 16 seconds; never reset the budget on an
  unchanged notification or duplicate exit.
- Serialize delayed retries. Discard callbacks for superseded sessions. Preserve
  a worker exit that arrives before the kickstart completion callback.
- Log numeric listener failure and bounded recovery/exhaustion in product logs.
- Preserve console ownership, signing, PAM/account verification, permissions,
  TLS, exclusive graphical ownership and retirement checks. Different-user
  desktop access still requires authentication as that desktop's owner.

Do not enable Network.framework's shared-endpoint reuse as an untested shortcut:
Apple documents that it includes both SO_REUSEADDR and SO_REUSEPORT. Recovery
must not permit overlapping listeners or kill an unrelated port owner.
Reference: https://developer.apple.com/documentation/network/nwparametersprovider/localendpointreuseallowed(_:)

## Validation

- Extend the real startup scheduling policy tests: success followed by bind
  failure/exit, exit before completion, wrong user/audit, duplicate notifications,
  finite retry exhaustion and fresh-session reset.
- Exercise delayed callback cancellation and duplicate scheduling with a
  synthetic coordinator fixture; never change launchd on a hosted builder.
- Build the native Mac Host on GitHub with all existing authentication,
  lifecycle, input, clipboard, transport and packaging assembly gates.
- Retest the actual sign-in-to-different-desktop-account sequence on an
  authorized installation. An unsigned CI assembly is not deployment acceptance.

The operator subsequently requested a unified test build with the Client
changelog. Both are merged into main for matching 1.0.146 packages; signing
authorization remains main-only. This recovery code itself changes no Linux,
Client or protocol behavior. Automated gates pass; live handoff acceptance
remains pending. No automatic deployment or GitHub release publication is part
of the unified test build. The separate Wallpaper hover-lag investigation
remains deferred.
